<article class="env-lemma" id="0C21">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0C21">Lemma <span data-tag="0C21">10.163.6</span>.</a> Let $\varphi : R \to S$ be a ring map. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$R$ is Noetherian, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$S$ is Noetherian 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\varphi $ is flat, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the fibre rings $S \otimes _ R \kappa (\mathfrak p)$ are reduced, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$R$ is reduced. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $S$ is reduced. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      For Noetherian rings reduced is the same as having properties $(S_1)$ and $(R_0)$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/031R" data-tag="031R">10.157.3</a>. Thus we know $R$ and the fibre rings have these properties. Hence we may apply Lemmas <a href="/tag/0339" data-tag="0339">10.163.4</a> and <a href="/tag/033A" data-tag="033A">10.163.5</a> and we see that $S$ is $(S_1)$ and $(R_0)$, in other words reduced by Lemma <a href="/tag/031R" data-tag="031R">10.157.3</a> again. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>